{
  "_comment": "Cross-domain bearing fault diagnosis pairs (FD-A/B/C/D, all 12 ordered pairs, see datasets.cfg cfg_fd{x}_fd{y}). Hub-and-spoke layout: one pretrain block per source domain, finetuning on the other three (mirrors the capture24→{WISDM,WISDM2} pattern in experiments.json) — covers all 12 pairs with only 4 pretrain runs per window size instead of 12. Two blocks per source domain, logsig+xf / mlp_logsig+bilinear, differing only in logsig_window_size (64 vs 128). 'None adjustment' baseline: logsig_lead_lag=0 and logsig_lag=0 (both left at their defaults, not swept). channel_adapt=none explicitly set (also the default) since all FD domains share the same 1-channel vibration signal layout, so no cross-dataset channel adaptation is needed. Cheap sweep budget (epochs_pretrain=2, epochs_finetune=10), seeds 0-9, run_modes=finetune,freeze,baseline — matches experiments_har70plus_harth.json. Run with: python scripts/run_experiments.py experiment_configs/experiments_fd_crossdomain.json --gpus 6,7,8",
